title: "US Care Safety Signals"
abstract: >-
  Analyses of public US federal data on injuries to caregivers and harm to
  patients during patient handling and transfer in hospitals and nursing
  facilities. Modules cover resident-handling injuries (5,654 of 25,860
  nursing-facility cases reported to OSHA for 2025), the handling task under
  way (about 1,440 hospital injuries during lateral transfers between
  surfaces), lifting equipment mentioned in injury narratives, injury rates
  per 100 full-time workers with a facility-level dataset of 7,554
  establishments, three-year trends for 2023-2025, cost estimates, violence
  against caregivers, patient harm in 14,439 FDA MAUDE reports for patient
  lifts, transfer devices, and stretchers (2015-2025), hospital-acquired
  pressure injury and HACRP penalties across 3,056 hospitals, graded
  crosswalks linking 8,047 OSHA establishments to CMS-certified nursing homes
  and 3,180 to CMS hospitals, an out-of-sample validation against OSHA's OIICS
  coding, and a pre-specified protocol for evaluating a change in how patients
  are moved. Every text-classification rule is validated against blind human
  review. Facilities are identified by federal identifier and state only; no
  product or manufacturer is named.
type: dataset
